    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="71">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 71</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ beon þa heregeata<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_71.lnote.oe.21"/> swa fundene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_71.lnote.oe.22"/>, swa<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_71.lnote.oe.1"/> hit mæðlic si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IICn_71.lnote.oe.23"/>:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>And beon ða herigeata swa gefundene, swa hit mæðlic sy:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="356" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ beon þa heregeate, swa hit mæðlic sy:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Et sint releuationes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_71.lnote.oe.13"/> ita inuentę, sicut modus sit:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Et illud debitum, quod heregeat supra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_71.lnote.oe.12"/> nominauimus, ita conuenienter pręparetur, secundum quod natus est:</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Exercitualia uero ita s[i]nt moderata, ut tollerabile sit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="71" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="208" ed="#robertson"/>And beon ða herigeata swa gefundene<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#IICn_71.robnote.fn.11"/> swa hit mæðlic sy.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="290" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And beon þa heregeata swa fundene, swa hit mæðlic si.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="357" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_71.lnote.de.1"/> es seien die Hergewæte so festgesetzt, wie es standesgemäss<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_71.lnote.de.2"/> ist:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let the heriots be fixed in such a way as befits [each one's] rank:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="209" ed="#robertson"/>Heriots shall be fixed with due regard to the rank of the person for whom they are paid.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="472" ed="#whitelock"/>And heriots are to be so determined as befits the rank:</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="291" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And a person’s tribute shall be assessed according to his status.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">‘fundene’ is a later bracketing in G and is missing in Ld.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 357, October 2026 (MS Cons); AY: corrected against Rabin p. 290, October 2026 (was “∅”, now “| eallswa: swa B”); AZ: corrected against Rabin p. 290, October 2026 (was “∅”, now “|”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">swa fundene: omitted A</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Eorles</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">eallswa: swa B</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">tribute: The heriot, that is, the military obligations, material, or financial support owed to the king.</note>
        <note type="translator" source="#rabin-doml">mancuses: A mancus is a gold coin worth roughly the equivalent of thirty pence.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sunt <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sunt Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">reuela. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">reuela. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-te <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-te Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">neu eingeklammert G; fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">bracketed by a modern hand in G; lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">356</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">357</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_71.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Benutzt, wie 71a, durch Hn 14, 1; übersetzt, aber mit bewusster Änderung und Fortlassung des Geldbetrags, durch Leis Wl II 20</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Used, like 71a, by Hn 14, 1; translated, but with deliberate alteration and omission of the sum of money, by Leis Wl II 20</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_71.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">211</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">In Cnuts Sinne, aber vielleicht nicht im Worte <hi rend="italic">mæðlic</hi>, liegt eine Ermässigung des Heergewæte; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 5a. Doch versteht auch C das Wort so, das allerdings diese Bed. haben <hi rend="spaced">kann</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cnut’s intention, but perhaps not the word <hi rend="italic">mæðlic</hi>, implies a reduction of the heriot; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 5a. Yet C too understands the word thus, and it admittedly <hi rend="italic">can</hi> have this meaning</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_71.robnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">208</biblScope></bibl><label>gefundene</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">swa fundene</hi> G; om. A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
